// Dark Skies DLC

TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.ResistCouncil.BrokenEarth=Captain, Royal Commonwealth Forces, ret. 2098; Case Officer, undisclosed location, Secret Intelligence Service, 2098-2099; SIS liaison to Australian Counterterrorism Center, 2100-2101; Chief of Station, Lagos, 2101-2103; Chief of Station, Rawalpindi, 2103-2105; Deputy Chief of African Affairs, 2105-2106; Senior adviser to insurgent group, location undisclosed, 2107-present.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.DestroyCouncil.BrokenEarth=Enlisted Paratrooper in Laredo War, awarded for bravery at Battle of Bristle Gap in 2084. Trained Pan-American Security Academy, 2087. Served as a line officer or adviser with various anti-separatist special operations units and militias in Venezuela, Panama, and Peru, in the 2080s. In 2107, briefly imprisoned in Buenos Aires on war crimes charges stemming from alleged activities during Operation Vulture in the early 2080s; acquitted in 2108.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.ExploitCouncil.BrokenEarth=Various positions with arms manufacturer Western Armories, 2096-present, including chairman of the board since 2106. Minority ownership stake in DWKY Industries, which has diamond mining partnerships with the governments of Botswana and Namibia. He is occasionally criticized in activist media for labor practices of his various interests, but no formal investigations are known to have taken place.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.EscapeCouncil.BrokenEarth=Master of Physics and Philosophy, University of Alexandria, 2100; Lead investor, Al Zaabi Satellite Communications; Deputy Director of Administration. Noted financial supporter of several space enthusiast organizations and publications.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.SubmitCouncil.BrokenEarth=Attended Southwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, Fort Worth, Texas, departed 2094 without degree. Charged with incitement and transporting controlled substances related to the mass suicide of members of the Eternal Source cult in Arizona in 2096; charges were later dropped. Worked as content manager for a collection of California-based New Age web sites predicting alien arrival in the coming decades, 2097-present, during which time she became a popular public speaker and self-help guru.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.AppeaseCouncil.BrokenEarth=B.A. in Political Science, University of Chennai, 2075, where he was a civil rights activist. Shot by police during a protest in Muzaffarnagar, Uttar Pradesh, in 2076. Resided in Vancouver, Canada, 2076-2082. Worked as civilian monitor for peacekeeping operations in various locations, including Baluchistan, Tamaulipas, and Moldova, 2082-2102. Master of Laws with a focus on international human rights law, Sydney University, 2084. Testified at war crimes tribunals as well as during prosecutions of peacekeepers who committed serious offenses during missions. Since 2102, he has served as an adviser to various human rights and peace organizations.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.CooperateCouncil.BrokenEarth=B.S., Astronautical Engineering; Tsinghua University, 2078; M.S. and PhD, Chemistry, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, 2082; PhD, Public Management, Tsinghua University, 2085; Professor of Science and Technology Policy and Management, Xi'an Jiaotong University, 2088-present; Director, C62 League, 2104-2107.
